      "writtenOn": "2017-11-28T20:26:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there is no need to add an environment variable equivalent here. The other OS_ variables are properties of the cloud, this is just a flag to turn on or off behavior.\n\nAlso, I don\u0027t think this is correct syntax for an argument that is just a boolean flag, you will need something like action\u003d\u0027store_true\u0027 or action\u003d\u0027store_false\u0027: https://docs.python.org/3/library/argparse.html#action\n\nProbably the default behavior should be to add the member role, so adding the flag should cause a store_false. In that case the flag should be be in the negative, so something like --no-add-member-role",
      "revId": "8be94ffc4d68e614d386d70f28acf3e39bafaf14",
